    "result_text": "The build is green. The suite's only test class (`AcceptanceTest`) passes, and the full `mvn test` reports BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` following the existing derived-field pattern (like `displayName`, `initials`, `customerCode`):\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient` derived getter `getMembershipNumber()` that returns `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of `registrationDate`'s year (`String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`). It returns `null` until both source fields are set.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `membershipNumber` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it (example `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nNo controller change was needed: `addOwner` already sets `registrationDate` (defaulting to today) and `customerCode` at creation, and MapStruct's `toOwnerDto` picks up the new getter automatically \u2014 so the value is derived purely from the owner's own fields and is seed-independent, exactly as the test requires.",
